sshpilot (6.4.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release v6.4.1.
  * Closing a connected tab asks once instead of twice; cancelling no
    longer leaves a session running with no tab
  * Quitting can be confirmed with the same "Don't ask me again" option
  * If the app crashes or is killed, its SSH sessions, forwards and
    transfers now stop with it instead of running on unreachable
  * Detach and restore-sessions-on-startup are retired: detached
    sessions could never be reopened, and restore never covered a crash
  * Settings: Interface is now General and holds Ask before closing a
    tab and Ask before quitting; Background Service moves to Advanced
    and shows the real idle shutdown time
  * The About dialog shows the bundled app icon, not an outdated system
    copy
  * Spanish: "Close" now reads "Cerrar"

 -- Mehdi <mah.fat@gmail.com>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:04:31 +0000

sshpilot (6.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release v6.4.0.
  * Saved hosts now connect exactly as `ssh <alias>` does in a terminal:
    earlier Host * and Match blocks, /etc/ssh/ssh_config and the main
    config of hosts in included files all apply as OpenSSH applies them
  * If a setting you typed is no longer the one used, a banner in the
    main window says so and the connection editor marks the field with
    the value that wins and where it comes from; open Effective Config
    for details
  * Saved passwords are looked up by the user and host OpenSSH resolves,
    so a Host * that changes User or HostName may ask for the password
    once more
  * The app keepalive is now only a fallback; a ServerAliveInterval in
    your SSH config wins
  * Host key checking is left to your SSH config unless you set it in
    Settings
  * Settings > SSH Options is now a page of overrides that win over the
    SSH config, with Not set by default, keyword suggestions, an address
    family option, a legacy device compatibility switch and free-form
    extra options
  * Clear messages when the SSH config cannot be read, is read-only, is
    a link the app cannot see, or is rejected by OpenSSH; no more .bak
    copy beside it
  * A linked ~/.ssh/config is followed the way OpenSSH does
  * File manager: Windows servers keep nested folders on upload and show
    their paths as the server gives them; Flatpak users get Request
    Access for folders the sandbox cannot reach
  * Dashboard keeps its data and tab while refreshing
  * New Colored Text style for sidebar group colours
  * RDP: gtk4-frdp 0.2.4, OpenSSL legacy provider bundled on Windows,
    FreeRDP diagnostics in the app log
  * Fixed a crash in the shortcuts overview, an X11 ibus crash when
    closing the SSH config editor, and a corrupt process registry after
    a power cut on Windows

